<BaseLayout title="Research & Publications | Bhagyashri Patil">
<header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Research / Publications / Exploration</span><h1>Stay curious.<br/><span class="accent">Keep building.</span></h1><p>From assistive technology to language and product review analytics, research has shaped how I formulate problems, analyze evidence, and connect technology to human needs.</p></header>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">01 / Graduate research</span><div><h2>Understanding products through customer feedback.</h2><p>During graduate study in Big Data Analytics at San Diego State University, I worked on research concerning Amazon product reviews, advised by Professor David Goldberg at SDSU's AI Research Lab.</p><p>The original research description explored how product-review patterns could identify potentially dysfunctional products, surface insights, and help inform customer purchasing decisions. These were research questions, not claims of a production platform.</p><p>Related interests included discourse analytics, topic modeling, semantic analysis, and natural language processing.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Earlier publications</span><div><h2>Assistive technology with a practical purpose.</h2><p>My undergraduate research at the University of Pune included a camera-based assistive system designed to read text and product labels for people with visual impairments.</p></div></div><div class="publication-grid"><article class="publication"><span class="eyebrow">Publication / 2016</span><h3>Camera-Based Assistive Text and Product Label Reading for Blind Person</h3><p>International Journal of Innovative Research and Creative Technology (IJIRCT).</p><a href="https://github.com/patilbp/patilbp.github.io/blob/archive/legacy-jekyll-2026-10-15/_pages/publications.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View archived citation ↗</a></article><article class="publication"><span class="eyebrow">Publication / 2015</span><h3>Camera-Based Assistive Text and Product Label Reading for Blind Person</h3><p>International Engineering Research Journal (IERJ).</p><a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Bhagyashri-Patil-6" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ResearchGate profile ↗</a></article></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Ongoing exploration</span><div><h2>Where cloud, product, and AI meet.</h2><p>I'm exploring questions about scalable architectures, intelligent workflows, retrieval-based applications, and the responsible use of AI in enterprise products. Future projects will document actual design choices and implementation evidence separately from learning interests.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/projects/">Explore projects ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/patilbp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
